{
 "about": "Automation of FL's global controls. An automation clip has a target and points [beat, value, tension?] counted in beats from the clip's start; it acts where it sits on the playlist. Tempo: value = (bpm - 60) / 120, so 0.5 is 120 BPM and 0.9167 is 170; here it climbs from 120 to 170 over four bars, then a tape stop drops it to 60 inside one bar. Master pitch ({global: main_pitch}): 0.5 is in tune and the knob spans an octave each way (0.25 = -6 semitones); the whole mix slides down a whole tone in the last two bars. The overall fade is the master insert's fader, {mixer: 0, param: vol}. {global: main_vol} also exists and is written, but FL 2025 ignores it: the level did not move, in a render or live.",
